        </parameterset>
        <parameterset type="modeParams" >
            <param name="mode" value="car" />
            <param name="constant" value="0.0" />
            <param name="marginalUtilityOfTraveling_util_hr" value="-6.0" />
            <param name="monetaryDistanceRate" value="-0.01" />
        </parameterset>
        <!-- Walk distance limit (2026-08-06): walk was the only mode with zero
             monetaryDistanceRate, and it showed: a check of a converged
             20-iteration run's output_trips.csv found mean walk trip distance
             7.8km, median 5.8km, with 21% of all walk trips over 10km (167,729
             walk trips total). Real people don't walk that far; walk needs a
             real cost like every other mode already has, not just its own
             (uncosted) travel-time disutility.
             Rate is not arbitrary: it's this project's own regulated shared-
             tricycle per-km marginal rate (TricycleFare.SHARED_PER_KM_RATE,
             PHP 2/km beyond the first 2km); i.e. walking a given distance is
             priced as if forgoing a real, already-affordable ride for that
             distance, which is the actual real-world tradeoff being modeled.
             Pure per-meter rate (no flat/base component) is deliberate: it
             keeps short walks cheap/unaffected while making long ones
             increasingly costly, rather than a hard distance cutoff (MATSim
             has no clean per-trip mode-eligibility hook; see
             PermissibleModesCalculator, which only operates per whole Plan;
             so a hard cutoff would require forking core MATSim replanning
             code; this is the safer lever). Verify effect empirically after
             a run, same as the car/motorcycle fuel-cost calibration. -->
        <parameterset type="modeParams" >
            <param name="mode" value="walk" />
            <param name="constant" value="0.0" />
            <param name="marginalUtilityOfTraveling_util_hr" value="-6.0" />
            <param name="monetaryDistanceRate" value="-0.002" />
        </parameterset>
